title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › Try a sample
route: /authorizations/eligibility/verify
intro: Seven small chips in a tinted strip at the foot of the form fill it with a member who ends in a different answer, so every verdict can be seen without a trick. The last four digits of the member ID script the answer. 'Authorization first' is J.M.'s card, the headline case R-1042. 'More samples' opens five more chips for the checks that need a look (next diagram).
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the endings are scripted. Typing the same ending by hand gives the same answer, on Verify and on the Coverage row in New Case.
---
start s1 "Open the Verify page"
screen sc "Strip 'Try a sample' at the foot of 'Patient and service'\nSeven small chips and 'More samples'"
decision qs "Is R-1042 (Site A) in the site view?"
process ps "'Authorization first' is left out: a Site B view never touches a Site A case"
decision q1 "Click which chip?"

group gPick "What each chip fills in"
  process p1 "'Cleared to bill'\nBeacon PPO, IOP, member ending 2468\nBeacon asks for no authorization for IOP"
  process p0 "'Authorization first'\nJ.M., 34, Summit Medicaid HMO, Residential 3.5, member SM7403964821\nThe check updates R-1042"
  process p2 "'Coverage lapsed'\nSummit Medicaid HMO, Residential 3.5, member ending 1012"
  process p3 "'Not found'\nLakeshore Behavioral, IOP, member ending 9999"
  process p4 "'Not covered'\nBeacon PPO, Residential 3.5, member ending 3030"
  process p5 "'Another plan pays first'\nSummit Medicaid HMO, IOP, member ending 6060"
  process p6 "'Limit reached'\nCardinal Health Plan, Residential 3.5, member ending 9090"
endgroup

process pf "Payer, member ID, date of birth, program and date of service are all filled\nThe chip turns green. 'Check now' is on"
click c1 "Click 'Check now'"
process ck "Live check runs about 10 seconds\nChips and fields lock. 'Skip ahead' speeds it up\nThe member ID ending decides the answer"

group gRes "Result: verdict, the fact behind it, rows"
  screen r1 "'Cleared to bill' · Authorization 'Not required'\nEligibility 'Eligible', Benefits 'Covered', Patient pays 'Copay $40 per day, ...'\n'Beacon does not require one for IOP · 10/21/2026 to 10/31/2026'"
  screen r0 "R-1042 · 'Authorization first' · Authorization 'In progress'\nButton 'Start authorization'"
  screen r2 "'Fix before billing' · Coverage 'Lapsed 10/12'\nEligibility 'Needs a fix', 'Effective 01/01/2026, lapsed 10/12/2026'\nButton 'Request retro-eligibility'"
  screen r3 "'Fix before billing' · Coverage 'Not found'\n'No coverage found for these details'; Benefits and What this service needs 'Not checked'\nNo 'Patient pays' row, no dates. Button 'Ask Caller to phone the payer'"
  screen r4 "'Fix before billing' · Benefits 'Not covered'\nRow 'The service is not covered' in the side panel's 'Payment checks'"
  screen r5 "'Fix before billing' · Other insurance 'Another plan pays first'\nRow 'Another plan pays first', chip 'Other plan', in the side panel"
  screen r6 "'Fix before billing' · Limit '14 of 14 days used'\nBenefits '... · All 14 days used'\nRow 'Every authorized day is used', chip 'Limit reached'"
endgroup

process sd "The list already holds a patient for each reason\nR-1101 lapsed, R-0975 ended, R-1118 not covered\nI-2275 another plan pays first, R-0921 limit reached"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Which verdict and why"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › List › What the screen shows"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › More samples: checks that need a look"

s1 --> sc --> qs
qs -->|Yes| q1
qs -->|No| ps --> q1
q1 -->|Cleared to bill| p1 --> pf
q1 -->|Authorization first| p0 --> pf
q1 -->|Coverage lapsed| p2 --> pf
q1 -->|Not found| p3 --> pf
q1 -->|Not covered| p4 --> pf
q1 -->|Another plan pays first| p5 --> pf
q1 -->|Limit reached| p6 --> pf
pf --> c1 --> ck
ck -->|Ends 2468| r1
ck -->|J.M.'s card| r0
ck -->|Ends 1012| r2
ck -->|Ends 9999| r3
ck -->|Ends 3030| r4
ck -->|Ends 6060| r5
ck -->|Ends 9090| r6
r1 & r0 & r2 & r3 & r4 & r5 & r6 --> g1
sc -.-> sd --> g2
sc -.-> g3
